A registration form first checks whether an age entry contains only digits. It converts the entry only after that check succeeds:

```python
entry = input("Age: ")
if entry.isdigit():
    age = int(entry)
    if age >= 18:
        print("Accepted")
    else:
        print("Must be 18 or older")
else:
    print("Digits only")
```

Which flat rewrite preserves all three outcomes without trying `int(entry)` on invalid text?
